WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.110
Avengers: Endgame officially confirmed that
Captain America is worthy of wielding the

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:09.700
mighty, mystical Mjolnir but the film didn't
explain why it took so long for the Star-Spangled

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.009
Avenger to summon the hammer, particularly
when he had the opportunity to do just that

00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:15.620
back in Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:19.960
Thanks to new intel from the masterminds behind
the biggest film of all time, we finally know

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.560
why Cap didn't lift Mjolnir until Endgame.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.800
During an Ask Me Anything session on Reddit,
the Russo Brothers fielded a question about

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:31.009
Captain America's ability to wield Mjolnir,
the square-headed sledgehammer only able to

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:34.280
be utilized by those the Asgardian gods believe
is worthy.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.520
"Whosoever be he worthy shall haveth the power!

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:38.940
Whatever, man.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.720
It's a trick."

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.580
Its most famous user is, of course, the Asgardian
God of Thunder Thor.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.850
Audiences got the first hint that Captain
America would be worthy of wielding the weapon

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.400
in Age of Ultron, when Thor invited the rest
of the Avengers to try their hand at lifting

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:52.900
Mjolnir.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:57.040
When Steve Rogers stepped up to the plate,
he was able to shift the hammer slightly,

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.480
unlike the rest of the crew, who couldn't
even make it budge.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.870
This caused Thor to perk up in his seat and
look visibly concerned that Steve would genuinely

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.780
end up swinging Mjolnir through the air.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.650
In Endgame, when Captain America summons Mjolnir
during the intense final battle against Thanos,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.640
"Bro Thor" is totally pumped:

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.340
"I knew it!"

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.680
This suggested that the God of Thunder had
known for years that Cap was worthy of wielding

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.400
the hammer likely recognizing that fact way
back in Age of Ultron.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:29.200
It subsequently caused many, including one
curious Reddit user, to wonder whether Captain

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:33.070
America could always wield Mjolnir, and was
thus able to lift it in Age of Ultron and

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:36.780
simply decided not to, or if he accrued worthiness
over time.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.440
Anthony Russo explained on Reddit that, in
his interpretation, Captain America "always

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.409
could" pick up Mjolnir, and realized that
during the party at Stark's place in Age of

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:45.960
Ultron.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:46.980
Anthony wrote,

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.340
"Our interpretation of the famous scene in
Ultron was that when he realized he could

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:54.400
pick up Mjolnir he quickly chose not to, because
he didn't want to embarrass Thor."

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.350
Why might Thor be embarrassed by his fellow
Avenger picking up and putting to use his

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.659
famous weapon, you ask?

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:03.940
Well, it's probably down to the fact that
anyone deemed worthy enough to wield Mjolnir

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.980
instantly obtains all the powers Thor has
when they lift it.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.079
Combine the abilities Mjolnir grants its users
with Captain America's super-strength, durability,

00:02:12.079 --> 00:02:16.170
and near-indestructible Vibranium shield and
it's easy to see why Thor might have gone

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.180
red in the face if Cap lifted Mjolnir in Age
of Ultron.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.680
Plus, there's the issue of Thor making a big
deal about being the so-called chosen one,

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.349
not an Earthly mortal like the rest of the
Avengers.

00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:28.740
He's obviously pretty attached to ol' Mjolnir:

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:31.360
"What am I looking at?"

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.640
"Sometimes it takes a while, give it a second."

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.419
Cap was sweet to save his Mjolnir-wielding
moment for Endgame, since it had much more

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:44.940
emotional heft and caused Thor to be joyful
instead of embarrassed.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.240
There was a huge payoff in watching Captain
America lay the smackdown on Thanos using

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.620
Mjolnir and his super-shield.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:54.760
The moment was certainly one of the most impactful
of the entire film, with audiences around

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.880
the world cheering in their seats when it
happened.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.950
Seeing Steve Rogers lift Mjolnir in Age of
Ultron could have been funny but watching

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.480
it happen in Endgame was infinitely more moving.

